1
00:03:15,886 --> 00:03:16,846
Mahabharatham.

2
00:03:18,206 --> 00:03:19,926
During the Pandavas' exile in disguise

3
00:03:20,326 --> 00:03:22,686
King Virata hit Yudhishthira with dice.

4
00:03:23,686 --> 00:03:29,006
For every drop of his royal blood,
the land would endure a year of drought.

5
00:03:30,006 --> 00:03:34,326
Knowing this, Mother Draupadi
caught the falling blood in her veil.

6
00:03:35,246 --> 00:03:37,126
Exposing their identity meant

7
00:03:37,366 --> 00:03:41,686
another twelve years
of exile in the forest.

8
00:03:42,406 --> 00:03:46,686
Yet, risking everything,
she thought only of her people's survival.

9
00:03:47,286 --> 00:03:50,206
Therefore, the people of Chittor believe
that worshipping her

10
00:03:50,366 --> 00:03:56,606
brings rain to this arid land,
which was once drenched

11
00:03:56,726 --> 00:03:58,326
in Lord Venkateswara’s own blood.

12
00:03:58,686 --> 00:04:03,326
So, they worship Draupadi every year.

13
00:04:04,766 --> 00:04:07,366
The Mahabharatham unfolds
across 18 volumes.

14
00:04:08,206 --> 00:04:09,726
The Kurukshetra war lasted for 18 days.

15
00:04:10,686 --> 00:04:15,366
Reflecting this, the 18-day
<i>Bharatham Mitta</i> festival is celebrated.

16
00:04:19,406 --> 00:04:22,086
This is <i>Bharatham Mitta</i>,
resembling a chariot.

17
00:04:28,646 --> 00:04:31,486
This holy place has
just one absolute rule.

18
00:04:32,086 --> 00:04:36,046
Not a single drop of blood
should be spilled on this soil.

19
00:04:40,806 --> 00:04:45,006
This is the story of an orphan
who arrived in this land, famished.

20
00:04:46,806 --> 00:04:47,926
Stop talking nonsense.

21
00:04:48,006 --> 00:04:50,646
Eguva Ramapuram hoists the flag.
That's the tradition.

22
00:04:50,966 --> 00:04:52,926
If Diguva Ramapuram hoists the flag
for a couple of years,

23
00:04:53,046 --> 00:04:54,206
that'll become the tradition from then on.

24
00:05:03,006 --> 00:05:04,006
Sir!

25
00:05:04,966 --> 00:05:07,486
I'm hungry. Can you please
give me some food?

26
00:05:07,966 --> 00:05:08,926
How could I?

27
00:05:09,446 --> 00:05:12,086
Both villages are fighting
to hoist the flag,

28
00:05:12,606 --> 00:05:15,046
hoping it will bring them good fortune.

29
00:05:16,326 --> 00:05:19,566
The food is offered to the deity
only after the flag has been hoisted

30
00:05:19,886 --> 00:05:20,806
and the serving of food begins.

31
00:05:21,126 --> 00:05:22,806
You'd better go stand in line.

32
00:06:07,766 --> 00:06:11,006
It's raining right after the hoisting,
for the first time in years!

33
00:06:12,046 --> 00:06:13,006
A good omen.

34
00:06:25,366 --> 00:06:26,366
Kid…

35
00:06:27,366 --> 00:06:28,366
Who are you?

36
00:06:31,246 --> 00:06:32,206
Where are your parents?

37
00:06:33,446 --> 00:06:34,766
I'm an orphan, Mother.

38
00:06:37,886 --> 00:06:40,486
How can you be an orphan
when you've called me Mother?

39
00:06:41,006 --> 00:06:42,126
Aren't we all with you?

40
00:06:42,926 --> 00:06:44,126
I'm so hungry, Mother.

41
00:06:45,446 --> 00:06:47,006
Oh, God. Vasanth.

42
00:06:47,286 --> 00:06:48,246
Coming, Mom.

43
00:06:57,686 --> 00:06:59,006
What's your name?

44
00:07:00,406 --> 00:07:01,366
His name…

45
00:07:33,686 --> 00:07:34,486
Come on in.

46
00:07:36,006 --> 00:07:37,806
Where's the jailer, brother?

47
00:07:38,126 --> 00:07:39,406
Apparently, there's a function
at his house,

48
00:07:39,686 --> 00:07:40,646
so he's running late.

49
00:07:41,206 --> 00:07:43,366
The jailer arranged your early release
because of your good nature.

50
00:07:44,006 --> 00:07:45,806
He'd already signed on your papers.

51
00:07:47,366 --> 00:07:48,246
All these days,

52
00:07:48,406 --> 00:07:51,766
you kept us hooked on the
Mahabharata.

53
00:07:52,126 --> 00:07:53,686
Now you're leaving without finishing it?

54
00:07:53,966 --> 00:07:55,726
I'm heading out to finish it, brother.

55
00:07:56,326 --> 00:07:57,686
You're heading out to finish it?

56
00:08:22,086 --> 00:08:22,926
- Sir.
- Yes.

57
00:08:23,126 --> 00:08:25,366
- Did the event go well, sir?
- It went well, Rajendra.

58
00:08:25,486 --> 00:08:27,206
Sir, about convict number 108…

59
00:08:27,886 --> 00:08:30,286
When asked why he was leaving
without finishing the Mahabharata,

60
00:08:30,726 --> 00:08:32,406
he said he is leaving
so he can conclude it.

61
00:08:32,566 --> 00:08:33,566
I didn’t get it, sir.

62
00:08:34,686 --> 00:08:35,486
Tell me this,

63
00:08:35,766 --> 00:08:37,566
did anyone
come to pick him up?

64
00:08:37,926 --> 00:08:39,686
No humans, sir. Just a dog!

65
00:08:43,206 --> 00:08:44,046
Kannaiah?

66
00:10:06,446 --> 00:10:07,366
Who is that?

67
00:10:10,366 --> 00:10:12,286
How are you, my son?

68
00:10:13,366 --> 00:10:15,406
Nobody even mentioned
you were getting released.

69
00:10:15,566 --> 00:10:16,886
I'm really hungry.

70
00:10:17,686 --> 00:10:18,806
Hurry up and bring me some food.

71
00:10:25,446 --> 00:10:26,806
I need you to look into a case.

72
00:10:26,966 --> 00:10:27,806
Of course, sir.

73
00:10:27,886 --> 00:10:29,046
I am sending over the details

74
00:10:29,326 --> 00:10:30,486
and addresses of a few people.

75
00:10:37,806 --> 00:10:38,806
What happened, sir?

76
00:10:39,366 --> 00:10:40,966
Something's about to happen.

77
00:10:48,566 --> 00:10:50,006
Go check on them
and see what they need.

78
00:10:50,046 --> 00:10:50,966
Okay, brother.

79
00:11:14,086 --> 00:11:14,926
Brother,

80
00:11:14,966 --> 00:11:16,566
the tables are full.

81
00:11:17,006 --> 00:11:19,126
Looking at this crowd,
they won't budge until they're done.

82
00:11:19,446 --> 00:11:20,446
I can get you a parcel if you want.

83
00:11:20,566 --> 00:11:21,366
Hey, Delhi!

84
00:11:21,966 --> 00:11:22,886
Let them be seated at my table.

85
00:11:23,446 --> 00:11:24,606
Attend to them personally.

86
00:11:34,006 --> 00:11:36,126
I'm seeing fear in your eyes
for the first time.

87
00:11:37,086 --> 00:11:37,926
Who is he?

88
00:11:39,366 --> 00:11:40,206
Lenin.

89
00:11:58,366 --> 00:11:59,206
Brother,

90
00:11:59,366 --> 00:12:01,686
I didn't see you before.
I'm from your village too.

91
00:12:01,766 --> 00:12:03,406
I'm not from your village.

92
00:12:09,686 --> 00:12:11,566
That's exactly
what everyone back home says.

93
00:12:13,726 --> 00:12:14,806
What do they say?

94
00:12:16,046 --> 00:12:16,966
I mean…

95
00:12:17,046 --> 00:12:18,366
Whenever your name comes up,

96
00:12:18,606 --> 00:12:20,766
they say you aren't one of us.

97
00:12:21,486 --> 00:12:22,326
Some people,

98
00:12:22,366 --> 00:12:23,766
curse just hearing your name.

99
00:12:24,686 --> 00:12:25,686
While others,

100
00:12:26,246 --> 00:12:27,366
get terrified.

101
00:12:28,086 --> 00:12:29,006
It's the same fear…

102
00:12:29,806 --> 00:12:31,366
I just saw in my boss's eyes.

103
00:12:32,326 --> 00:12:33,246
Who are you, brother?

104
00:12:34,566 --> 00:12:35,966
The whole village claims

105
00:12:36,766 --> 00:12:38,006
your chapter is closed.

106
00:12:38,686 --> 00:12:40,006
If your chapter is truly closed,

107
00:12:40,406 --> 00:12:41,686
why are you back?

108
00:12:44,766 --> 00:12:47,006
They're afraid to even utter the name,
the 100th <i>Bharatham Mitta.</i>

109
00:12:47,806 --> 00:12:49,006
What happened there?

110
00:12:56,366 --> 00:12:57,486
The Kurukshetra.

111
00:13:03,046 --> 00:13:05,206
To tell you about the Kurukshetra,

112
00:13:06,126 --> 00:13:09,606
it all begins with the death
of our village elder, Nadamuni.

113
00:13:11,486 --> 00:13:14,206
Bharatham Mitta begins only after

114
00:13:14,486 --> 00:13:16,566
this household's woman makes
the sacred offerings.

115
00:13:17,446 --> 00:13:18,606
It's all over now.

116
00:13:18,646 --> 00:13:19,686
Death may have struck our home,

117
00:13:21,006 --> 00:13:22,486
but <i>Bharatham Mitta</i>
serves the entire village.

118
00:13:23,406 --> 00:13:24,966
The tradition must continue
for the sake of people.

119
00:13:25,886 --> 00:13:26,886
We must keep it alive.

120
00:13:27,006 --> 00:13:30,726
From that day,
Jayyamma never removes her vermillion

121
00:13:31,326 --> 00:13:32,646
until the festival ends.

122
00:13:35,726 --> 00:13:37,406
The most revered title
in this entire festival is

123
00:13:37,446 --> 00:13:38,566
Dharma Raju!

124
00:13:38,806 --> 00:13:41,646
He is the king of <i>Bharatham Mitta.</i>

125
00:13:43,566 --> 00:13:45,606
Every household in the village
gets a turn to become Dharma Raju.

126
00:13:46,206 --> 00:13:47,406
After the festival,

127
00:13:47,486 --> 00:13:50,366
they adopt "Dharma Raju" as their surname.

128
00:13:52,446 --> 00:13:56,086
This is the ultimate recognition
that everyone craves.

129
00:13:56,926 --> 00:13:59,766
Especially, our uncle Ethirajulu.

130
00:14:00,766 --> 00:14:02,366
I have decided to play Dharma Raju

131
00:14:02,806 --> 00:14:04,246
for this upcoming festival.

132
00:14:04,726 --> 00:14:06,366
That is for us to decide.

133
00:14:06,926 --> 00:14:09,126
When will you decide?
When will I ever get my turn?

134
00:14:09,286 --> 00:14:10,286
What is this, sister-in-law?

135
00:14:10,366 --> 00:14:11,366
Who are you calling, sister-in-law?

136
00:14:11,606 --> 00:14:12,446
And who are you calling brother?

137
00:14:12,566 --> 00:14:14,046
You are nothing
but my father-in-law's illegitimate son!

138
00:14:15,326 --> 00:14:16,886
When your very birth is illegitimate,

139
00:14:17,046 --> 00:14:18,366
how dare you dream of playing Dharma Raju?

140
00:14:21,926 --> 00:14:23,246
As long as my family lives on,

141
00:14:23,686 --> 00:14:24,766
you will never be granted that honor.

142
00:14:26,086 --> 00:14:27,006
You drunkard!

143
00:14:27,726 --> 00:14:28,646
Get lost!

144
00:14:29,406 --> 00:14:31,086
Mother is generous to everyone.

145
00:14:31,606 --> 00:14:34,286
Ethirajulu is the only one
she's strict with.

146
00:14:37,086 --> 00:14:39,086
He is our Neelakantam uncle.

147
00:14:39,686 --> 00:14:41,246
The elder of Diguvaramapuram village.

148
00:14:41,926 --> 00:14:42,966
The man has a heart of gold.

149
00:14:47,486 --> 00:14:50,326
The Shakuni of this Bharatham.

150
00:14:50,766 --> 00:14:51,646
Damodaram.

151
00:14:52,126 --> 00:14:52,966
Brother-in-law,

152
00:14:53,006 --> 00:14:55,286
this wig finally works for you.

153
00:14:55,366 --> 00:14:56,406
Just like me,

154
00:14:56,966 --> 00:14:59,486
Kannaiah came to me
starving at last year's fair.

155
00:15:00,006 --> 00:15:01,046
My Kannaiah.

156
00:15:01,646 --> 00:15:02,646
And Balaji.

157
00:15:03,006 --> 00:15:03,966
Srinivasulu.

158
00:15:04,126 --> 00:15:04,966
Dwaraka.

159
00:15:05,006 --> 00:15:05,766
Murali.

160
00:15:06,006 --> 00:15:06,966
They're my whole world.

161
00:15:07,006 --> 00:15:08,566
The auspicious hour is slipping away!

162
00:15:08,726 --> 00:15:10,966
Dharma Raju is arriving
with the offerings.

163
00:15:11,086 --> 00:15:12,206
Where on earth are you?

164
00:16:12,886 --> 00:16:17,406
A Ravana descended
upon our joyful festival.

165
00:16:17,686 --> 00:16:20,046
- MLA Raghava Reddy.
- The MLA's cutout looks great.

166
00:16:20,766 --> 00:16:21,966
What is this, Damodaram?

167
00:16:24,406 --> 00:16:28,086
Why are you dragging politics
and cutouts onto this sacred land?

168
00:16:29,606 --> 00:16:31,366
You know we have our traditions, right?

169
00:16:31,406 --> 00:16:32,326
Oh, wow!

170
00:16:33,046 --> 00:16:36,006
Look who's lecturing us on tradition…
a widow who still dares to wear a bindi.

171
00:16:47,086 --> 00:16:48,126
Why did you lower your head,

172
00:16:48,806 --> 00:16:49,806
Mother?

173
00:16:51,766 --> 00:16:54,806
The heavens themselves
blessed your sacred status with rain.

174
00:16:56,726 --> 00:16:57,686
How can we

175
00:16:58,646 --> 00:17:01,606
just stand by
while a good-for-nothing insults you?

176
00:17:02,926 --> 00:17:05,246
We will hold our heads high
and crush anyone who gets in our way.

177
00:17:08,006 --> 00:17:09,606
You really think you can
take down my brother’s cutout?

178
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:11,406
Step forward if you dare.

179
00:17:12,206 --> 00:17:13,446
This will turn into a bloodbath.

180
00:17:15,606 --> 00:17:17,126
No blood should spill on this land.

181
00:17:18,446 --> 00:17:19,246
Whether it’s mine,

182
00:17:20,006 --> 00:17:22,286
yours, or your brother's…

183
00:17:23,686 --> 00:17:24,526
Listen to me.

184
00:17:24,806 --> 00:17:25,806
Take the cutout down.

185
00:17:26,086 --> 00:17:26,966
What if I don't?

186
00:17:30,206 --> 00:17:31,046
What will you do?

187
00:17:33,126 --> 00:17:34,246
What?

188
00:17:36,126 --> 00:17:37,326
Who do you think you are?

189
00:17:37,366 --> 00:17:39,566
- What if I don't?
- I'll take it down.

190
00:17:45,766 --> 00:17:46,686
Hey.

191
00:17:47,126 --> 00:17:48,246
He says he'll take it down!

192
00:17:50,646 --> 00:17:52,286
You pathetic loser!

193
00:17:53,806 --> 00:17:55,366
What gives you so much confidence?

194
00:17:55,686 --> 00:17:57,006
You think this crowd's got your back?

195
00:17:57,566 --> 00:17:58,686
Go ahead. Touch me.

196
00:17:59,366 --> 00:18:01,006
Let's see who's got your back.

197
00:18:02,966 --> 00:18:03,726
Hey!

198
00:18:04,086 --> 00:18:05,246
You go ahead!

199
00:18:57,366 --> 00:18:59,606
If his strength comes
from the position he holds,

200
00:19:00,406 --> 00:19:02,806
my faith lies in the village
standing right behind me.

201
00:19:08,806 --> 00:19:09,966
In any age,

202
00:19:10,486 --> 00:19:12,006
the one who acts righteous is Rama,

203
00:19:12,606 --> 00:19:14,126
and the one who spreads evil is Ravana.

204
00:19:16,046 --> 00:19:17,726
And by burning away that evil,

205
00:19:18,686 --> 00:19:21,766
the landmark 100th
<i>Bharatham Mitta</i> began in all its glory.

206
00:19:22,046 --> 00:19:24,646
<i>♪ It's the end of Ravana ♪</i>

207
00:19:24,686 --> 00:19:28,326
<i>♪ It's the end of Ravana ♪</i>

208
00:19:32,366 --> 00:19:35,966
<i>♪ It's the end of Ravana's reign ♪</i>

209
00:19:36,086 --> 00:19:39,646
<i>♪ It's the end of Ravana's reign ♪</i>

210
00:19:39,686 --> 00:19:43,326
<i>♪ It's the end of Ravana's reign</i>
<i>A celebration wrapped in glory ♪</i>

211
00:19:43,406 --> 00:19:46,966
<i>♪ A carnival bursting with vibrant hues ♪</i>

212
00:19:47,006 --> 00:19:50,566
<i>♪ Come, let us leap</i>
<i>And dance to the rhythm! ♪</i>

213
00:19:53,766 --> 00:19:55,966
<i>♪ A single raindrop</i>
<i>Falling on this sacred hill ♪</i>

214
00:19:56,006 --> 00:19:57,966
<i>♪ Can soften every waiting heart ♪</i>

215
00:20:01,286 --> 00:20:04,886
<i>♪ May the heavens</i>
<i>Shower us with rainy boons ♪</i>

216
00:20:04,966 --> 00:20:08,406
<i>♪ For our Mother Goddess</i>
<i>Is our true refuge ♪</i>

217
00:20:08,606 --> 00:20:12,286
<i>♪ Our future rests in her loving grace ♪</i>

218
00:20:12,326 --> 00:20:15,966
<i>♪ Let us honor Mother Draupadi</i>
<i>As our tradition has always taught ♪</i>

219
00:20:16,006 --> 00:20:20,006
<i>♪ Let us relive the grand epic</i>
<i>Of Mahabharata again and again!</i>

220
00:20:20,246 --> 00:20:21,966
<i>♪ It's the end ♪</i>

221
00:20:22,046 --> 00:20:23,726
<i>♪ It's the end ♪</i>

222
00:20:23,926 --> 00:20:27,366
<i>♪ It's the end of Ravana's reign ♪</i>

223
00:20:31,126 --> 00:20:34,686
<i>♪ It's the end of Ravana's reign ♪</i>

224
00:20:38,366 --> 00:20:39,926
<i>♪ May Lord Dharmaraja bless your path ♪</i>

225
00:20:39,966 --> 00:20:41,926
<i>♪ May Mother Draupadi shower her grace ♪</i>

226
00:20:42,046 --> 00:20:43,806
<i>♪ Noble at heart, blessed from birth ♪</i>

227
00:20:43,886 --> 00:20:45,686
<i>♪ Raised within your village's embrace ♪</i>

228
00:20:45,686 --> 00:20:49,406
<i>♪ Nurtured by Bharatham Mitta</i>
<i>The land of endless compassion ♪</i>

229
00:20:49,446 --> 00:20:53,006
<i>♪ Live a hundred glorious years</i>
<i>Like Nandagopala of Repalle ♪</i>

230
00:20:53,046 --> 00:20:56,686
<i>♪ Live a hundred glorious years</i>
<i>Like Nandagopala of Repalle ♪</i>

231
00:21:11,686 --> 00:21:15,366
<i>♪ This sacred vigil comes</i>
<i>But once a year ♪</i>

232
00:21:15,446 --> 00:21:18,926
<i>♪ Where the Goddess</i>
<i>Answers countless prayers ♪</i>

233
00:21:19,126 --> 00:21:22,606
<i>♪ Beneath Her loving gaze</i>
<i>The skies pour down in torrents ♪</i>

234
00:21:22,806 --> 00:21:26,326
<i>♪ Under Her gentle shade</i>
<i>The earth blooms in lush green ♪</i>

235
00:21:26,446 --> 00:21:28,126
<i>♪ How ancient is this sacred tradition? ♪</i>

236
00:21:30,126 --> 00:21:32,006
<i>♪ It has thrived</i>
<i>Through generations untold ♪</i>

237
00:21:33,886 --> 00:21:37,486
<i>♪ This soil has never been stained</i>
<i>By blood, dear brother ♪</i>

238
00:21:37,566 --> 00:21:40,686
<i>♪ Our story was never carved by swords ♪</i>

239
00:21:40,686 --> 00:21:44,886
<i>♪ Let us stand guard for all of time</i>
<i>And protect this sacred land! ♪</i>

240
00:21:45,006 --> 00:21:48,366
<i>♪ It's the end of Ravana's reign ♪</i>

241
00:21:52,286 --> 00:21:55,886
<i>♪ It's the end of Ravana's reign ♪</i>

242
00:21:59,406 --> 00:22:01,006
<i>♪ May Lord Dharmaraja bless your path ♪</i>

243
00:22:01,046 --> 00:22:02,926
<i>♪ May Mother Draupadi shower her grace ♪</i>

244
00:22:03,126 --> 00:22:05,046
<i>♪ Noble at heart, blessed from birth ♪</i>

245
00:22:05,086 --> 00:22:06,806
<i>♪ Raised within your village's embrace ♪</i>

246
00:22:06,886 --> 00:22:10,566
<i>♪ Nurtured by Bharatham Mitta</i>
<i>The land of endless compassion ♪</i>

247
00:22:10,606 --> 00:22:14,086
<i>♪ Live a hundred glorious years</i>
<i>Like Nandagopala of Repalle ♪</i>

248
00:22:14,206 --> 00:22:18,046
<i>♪ Live a hundred glorious years</i>
<i>Like Nandagopala of Repalle ♪</i>

249
00:22:21,766 --> 00:22:22,966
Hand it to the PA.

250
00:22:26,006 --> 00:22:26,966
Forgive me, brother.

251
00:22:27,086 --> 00:22:28,406
The entire village backed him yesterday.

252
00:22:28,446 --> 00:22:29,286
We couldn't stop them.

253
00:22:29,326 --> 00:22:30,886
One word
and I'll hack him down in broad daylight.

254
00:22:31,646 --> 00:22:32,406
Hey,

255
00:22:32,886 --> 00:22:33,886
it's election season.

256
00:22:34,366 --> 00:22:35,886
Act in haste and we lose everything.

257
00:22:37,286 --> 00:22:39,006
First, we must reclaim
our stripped respect.

258
00:22:42,646 --> 00:22:43,926
- What is it, Damodaram?
- Brother…

259
00:22:44,446 --> 00:22:46,206
No blood should be spilled
on that sacred land, right?

260
00:22:46,766 --> 00:22:47,806
It mustn't.

261
00:22:50,406 --> 00:22:52,606
Then I will make sure it will.

262
00:22:55,726 --> 00:22:58,286
Dear devotees and believers…

263
00:22:58,566 --> 00:23:00,006
Do you think Mother Draupadi's

264
00:23:00,126 --> 00:23:02,366
legacy
is merely about her beauty?

265
00:23:02,766 --> 00:23:03,926
Absolutely not.

266
00:23:04,086 --> 00:23:05,046
Her every smile,

267
00:23:05,246 --> 00:23:06,206
her every step,

268
00:23:06,326 --> 00:23:08,006
and her every action
defines cosmic righteousness.

269
00:23:14,286 --> 00:23:15,646
- Hey!
- My Ice cream…

270
00:23:15,686 --> 00:23:17,046
Why are you crying like that?

271
00:23:17,286 --> 00:23:19,686
Some girl snatched away my ice cream.

272
00:23:19,726 --> 00:23:21,966
Forget that thieving wench.
I’ll buy you another one.

273
00:23:22,006 --> 00:23:23,926
But he already gobbled up
all the remaining ones.

274
00:23:24,646 --> 00:23:26,206
Hey, hey.

275
00:23:26,406 --> 00:23:28,246
Stop crying like the sky is falling.

276
00:23:28,366 --> 00:23:29,566
Let's go track her down.

277
00:23:31,126 --> 00:23:31,966
Hey!

278
00:23:32,246 --> 00:23:34,606
Wipe your tears
and describe what she looks like.

279
00:23:34,686 --> 00:23:36,886
I don't know, brother.

280
00:23:37,246 --> 00:23:39,686
She stole berries
the day before yesterday.

281
00:23:42,246 --> 00:23:44,246
Yesterday, she stole a sugar bar.

282
00:23:45,886 --> 00:23:47,286
Today, it's ice.

283
00:23:49,486 --> 00:23:53,126
Do you know how good that ice tastes?

284
00:23:53,246 --> 00:23:54,006
Hey!

285
00:23:54,086 --> 00:23:55,766
Drop the food descriptions for a second

286
00:23:56,006 --> 00:23:57,486
and tell me the color of her outfit!

287
00:23:58,646 --> 00:24:00,006
She's wearing a green saree.

288
00:24:00,246 --> 00:24:02,486
With orange flowers in her hair.

289
00:24:03,006 --> 00:24:05,126
Now that’s a real clue.
Let’s go find her!

290
00:24:06,646 --> 00:24:07,406
Hey,

291
00:24:07,446 --> 00:24:08,566
- we are up next.
- Hey.

292
00:24:08,606 --> 00:24:10,126
It's about time. Let’s go!

293
00:24:14,126 --> 00:24:15,206
Move fast, brother!

294
00:24:15,606 --> 00:24:16,566
Hey, come on!

295
00:24:18,246 --> 00:24:19,686
Brother, it's this saree!

296
00:24:19,686 --> 00:24:20,966
- This one?
- Yes, this is it!

297
00:24:31,486 --> 00:24:32,366
O Duryodhana!

298
00:24:32,686 --> 00:24:35,406
Did you see
a girl in this costume pass by?

299
00:24:37,446 --> 00:24:38,286
What do you mean by "why"?

300
00:24:38,326 --> 00:24:40,726
She stole this kid's ice cream!
That basket-faced wench!

301
00:24:41,486 --> 00:24:43,366
- I need to teach her a lesson.
- Basket-faced?

302
00:24:43,726 --> 00:24:45,126
Did you see her or not?

303
00:24:46,446 --> 00:24:47,326
Hey.

304
00:24:47,686 --> 00:24:49,606
I'm talking to you!
Did you see her?

305
00:24:52,486 --> 00:24:53,926
I just saw her heading that way.

306
00:24:55,646 --> 00:24:56,486
Hey, come on.

307
00:24:56,606 --> 00:24:57,686
Let's go teach her a lesson.

308
00:25:16,806 --> 00:25:18,966
While the Pandavas lived in exile,

309
00:25:19,446 --> 00:25:22,686
King Virata boasted
about his son Uttara's immense bravery.

310
00:25:22,806 --> 00:25:24,806
But when Dharma Raju
credited Brihannala instead,

311
00:25:25,006 --> 00:25:27,486
the king lost his temper.

312
00:25:27,686 --> 00:25:31,566
In a fit of blind rage,
King Virata grabbed the dice

313
00:25:31,726 --> 00:25:33,006
and hurled them at Dharma Raju.

314
00:25:33,806 --> 00:25:36,686
Flying faster than the wind,

315
00:25:38,886 --> 00:25:41,046
they struck the noble king's forehead.

316
00:26:34,646 --> 00:26:36,486
She's leaving. Stop her, brother!

317
00:26:36,646 --> 00:26:37,406
Brother,

318
00:26:37,446 --> 00:26:39,566
that's her!
She stole my ice cream.

319
00:26:39,606 --> 00:26:40,566
You're here?

320
00:26:40,686 --> 00:26:44,126
You've had mumps and a fever all week,
and you ate a whole cart of ice cream?

321
00:26:44,246 --> 00:26:45,366
I'll teach you a lesson once we're home.

322
00:26:45,446 --> 00:26:47,926
- Mom, I didn't eat much. I only had one.
- Shut up.

323
00:26:51,006 --> 00:26:52,366
What did you say?

324
00:26:53,126 --> 00:26:54,646
Are you saying the son of a charioteer

325
00:26:54,686 --> 00:26:56,086
has no right to stand here,
just because of his race?

326
00:26:56,206 --> 00:26:58,486
What outrageous words!
What shocking words!

327
00:26:59,006 --> 00:27:01,686
This is a test of skill in battle
not a test of noble birth.

328
00:27:02,006 --> 00:27:03,286
No! It must not be so.

329
00:27:03,366 --> 00:27:04,966
Are you saying this is a test of community?

330
00:27:05,046 --> 00:27:07,086
Then What was the origin
of your own father, Bharadwaja?

331
00:27:07,206 --> 00:27:09,206
And what of your own disgraceful birth?

332
00:27:09,646 --> 00:27:11,126
Were you not born in a clay pot?

333
00:27:12,006 --> 00:27:13,686
Tell me then,
which community do you belong to?

334
00:27:18,486 --> 00:27:20,206
Her name is Bharathi.

335
00:27:20,406 --> 00:27:22,246
Neelakantam's younger daughter.

336
00:27:26,806 --> 00:27:28,086
I’ve never seen her around.

337
00:27:28,566 --> 00:27:29,886
How could you?

338
00:27:30,006 --> 00:27:31,046
She lives in Madras.

339
00:27:31,126 --> 00:27:33,966
Her uncle has no children of his own,
so he raised her since childhood.

340
00:27:34,326 --> 00:27:35,766
She looks traditional, right?

341
00:27:37,686 --> 00:27:39,006
She looks so precious.

342
00:27:46,886 --> 00:27:48,486
She completely nailed the performance.

343
00:27:48,606 --> 00:27:50,006
- Everyone is raving about it.
- Brother.

344
00:27:50,326 --> 00:27:51,086
Wow!

345
00:27:51,126 --> 00:27:52,446
Your dialogue delivery was flawless.

346
00:27:52,566 --> 00:27:54,366
You made me proud.

347
00:27:54,686 --> 00:27:55,446
See?

348
00:27:55,486 --> 00:27:57,686
Bharati is the one who will always
safeguard our family's honor.

349
00:27:57,886 --> 00:27:59,206
And you just sit around like a slacker,

350
00:27:59,406 --> 00:28:01,686
tying wish-fulfilling slips to that tree!

351
00:28:01,926 --> 00:28:04,406
- How dare you! Stop right there.
- Dad! Wait.

352
00:28:04,446 --> 00:28:06,206
- Dad.
- Wait.

353
00:28:06,326 --> 00:28:08,366
- She’s calling me a slacker.
- Hold on.

354
00:28:08,606 --> 00:28:09,806
Fine, fine, I’m sorry.

355
00:28:10,086 --> 00:28:11,006
Shall we head home now?

356
00:28:11,246 --> 00:28:12,726
Weren't you playing Duryodhana?

357
00:28:12,886 --> 00:28:13,926
Go on your own.

358
00:28:16,326 --> 00:28:17,326
Shall we go home, Dad?

359
00:28:18,006 --> 00:28:20,126
Your mother and I
have some unfinished work here.

360
00:28:20,286 --> 00:28:21,366
- Yes.
- I'll send someone to drop you.

361
00:28:21,446 --> 00:28:24,006
- Who else is here, Mom?
- Let him find someone.

362
00:28:24,046 --> 00:28:24,966
Lenin.

363
00:28:27,606 --> 00:28:28,646
Come here for a moment.

364
00:28:43,646 --> 00:28:44,806
She's my younger daughter, Bharathi.

365
00:28:45,206 --> 00:28:46,246
Please drop her off at home.

366
00:28:46,686 --> 00:28:47,966
- Okay, Uncle.
- He has a lot of work here.

367
00:28:48,086 --> 00:28:50,686
- I'll drop her off instead.
- Hey, it can wait.

368
00:28:50,766 --> 00:28:52,286
Hey, I said I'll drop her.

369
00:28:52,726 --> 00:28:54,446
Take my sister home.

370
00:28:54,726 --> 00:28:56,686
- Look at you blushing, brother!
- It's nothing like that.

371
00:28:56,766 --> 00:28:58,046
- Just go already.
- We get it.

372
00:28:58,246 --> 00:28:59,006
- Dude!
- Yes.

373
00:28:59,046 --> 00:29:01,086
- I'll drop her safely.
- Okay, careful.

374
00:29:01,326 --> 00:29:02,566
- Okay.
- Dear, go on.

375
00:29:02,606 --> 00:29:03,366
Be careful, dear.

376
00:29:03,686 --> 00:29:04,486
Come on.

377
00:29:11,566 --> 00:29:12,486
Stop staring.

378
00:29:13,006 --> 00:29:14,686
Anyway, how was my performance?

379
00:29:15,486 --> 00:29:17,006
Not quite up to NTR's level,

380
00:29:17,446 --> 00:29:18,646
but you did a solid job.

381
00:29:19,086 --> 00:29:20,086
I already know that.

382
00:29:20,686 --> 00:29:22,086
- So, what exactly do you do?
- Me?

383
00:29:22,326 --> 00:29:24,246
I’m the organizer of <i>Bharatham Mitta.</i>

384
00:29:25,246 --> 00:29:26,366
Organizer?

385
00:29:26,686 --> 00:29:29,766
So is your job chauffeuring girls home?

386
00:29:30,006 --> 00:29:30,886
Hey!

387
00:29:30,966 --> 00:29:32,326
Watch your mouth.

388
00:29:32,606 --> 00:29:34,006
This Lenin is pure as fire.

389
00:29:38,286 --> 00:29:40,086
Oh, look at that.

390
00:29:40,206 --> 00:29:42,206
- Mr. Fire's bike has broken down.
- It broke down?

391
00:29:42,366 --> 00:29:43,206
Yes.

392
00:29:44,046 --> 00:29:45,006
Hold this.

393
00:29:48,086 --> 00:29:48,926
Ouch!

394
00:29:50,006 --> 00:29:51,046
Watch now.

395
00:29:59,606 --> 00:30:00,446
Let's go.

396
00:30:03,006 --> 00:30:04,326
I just got it serviced the other day.

397
00:30:07,006 --> 00:30:08,726
- It broke down again?
- No.

398
00:30:09,286 --> 00:30:10,406
We've reached my house.

399
00:30:11,286 --> 00:30:12,086
Phew!

400
00:30:13,606 --> 00:30:15,126
A bike doesn't always stop
because it needs repairs.

401
00:30:15,246 --> 00:30:17,006
Sometimes, it stops because of Bharati.

402
00:30:17,286 --> 00:30:18,366
- Huh?
- Go now.

403
00:30:19,286 --> 00:30:20,086
Hey,

404
00:30:20,606 --> 00:30:21,486
take this with you.

405
00:30:30,366 --> 00:30:32,686
The <i>Bharatham Mitta</i>
started four days ago.

406
00:30:32,806 --> 00:30:33,926
These young punks
only show up to check out the girls.

407
00:30:34,006 --> 00:30:34,886
Yes. Let's go. Let's go.

408
00:30:34,926 --> 00:30:36,566
Not a single soul
drops money into the donation box.

409
00:30:36,726 --> 00:30:38,726
The procession of the
Iron God has begun.

410
00:30:38,926 --> 00:30:40,326
Pray and place
your offering in the donation box.

411
00:30:40,366 --> 00:30:41,366
- Amara.
- Brother?

412
00:30:41,366 --> 00:30:43,806
I gave him something to do.
Let's go sit down.

413
00:30:44,006 --> 00:30:48,446
A boy in a blue shirt
and brown shorts is lost. I request…

414
00:30:48,566 --> 00:30:49,926
Brother, give me your hand.

415
00:30:55,406 --> 00:30:56,926
Whoa! My nephew is kicking!

416
00:30:57,686 --> 00:31:00,286
If you don't marry soon
and bring a bride for him,

417
00:31:00,726 --> 00:31:01,886
he won't spare you.

418
00:31:01,926 --> 00:31:02,686
Wow!

419
00:31:04,286 --> 00:31:06,046
Do you expect me
to go chasing after girls now?

420
00:31:06,766 --> 00:31:07,606
Hey!

421
00:31:11,086 --> 00:31:12,366
Bharathi! Stop!

422
00:31:12,606 --> 00:31:13,926
Hey! What happened?

423
00:31:14,006 --> 00:31:15,726
Why are you chasing her?

424
00:31:15,806 --> 00:31:17,326
The husband of their maid, Ratna,

425
00:31:17,366 --> 00:31:19,566
gambled away her bangles
in a game with my brother-in-law.

426
00:31:19,606 --> 00:31:21,006
This girl just stormed in
and snatched them away.

427
00:31:21,966 --> 00:31:23,606
What are you doing?
Give them back.

428
00:31:25,006 --> 00:31:26,366
- I said do it.
- No. I won't!

429
00:31:26,446 --> 00:31:27,686
You keep stealing one thing or the other.

430
00:31:27,966 --> 00:31:28,726
Come on.

431
00:31:30,766 --> 00:31:31,806
What is your problem?

432
00:31:32,006 --> 00:31:33,486
You stole the bangles like a thief.

433
00:31:34,046 --> 00:31:35,606
You should win them back fairly,
like a man.

434
00:31:36,366 --> 00:31:38,126
Did anyone ever win against you?

435
00:31:41,006 --> 00:31:43,286
Oh, you're a tough guy
who tore down a poster.

436
00:31:43,806 --> 00:31:44,766
You want to play?

437
00:31:45,326 --> 00:31:46,366
Care for a game?

438
00:31:46,566 --> 00:31:48,446
He's afraid, brother-in-law.
Let him go.

439
00:31:49,646 --> 00:31:50,886
If he's scared, then forget it!

440
00:31:53,046 --> 00:31:53,886
He will play!

441
00:31:53,926 --> 00:31:54,886
What are the stakes?

442
00:31:56,406 --> 00:31:57,766
Why are you involving me?

443
00:31:57,806 --> 00:31:58,886
I don't even know how to play!

444
00:32:04,126 --> 00:32:05,126
Hey, Lenin.

445
00:32:05,726 --> 00:32:07,326
Do you honestly believe
you can beat me?

446
00:32:08,206 --> 00:32:09,806
Why would Lenin
waste his time beating you?

447
00:32:10,406 --> 00:32:11,286
I'm more than enough.

448
00:32:11,446 --> 00:32:12,326
Name the stakes.

449
00:32:12,566 --> 00:32:13,566
What do you want?

450
00:32:14,926 --> 00:32:17,646
Lenin must hand over complete management

451
00:32:18,086 --> 00:32:19,966
of the <i>Bharatham Mitta</i> to me this year.

452
00:32:26,766 --> 00:32:27,886
That is never going to happen.

453
00:32:28,086 --> 00:32:29,686
And since I'm going to win anyway,

454
00:32:30,366 --> 00:32:32,766
you must completely
ban gambling this year.

455
00:32:33,366 --> 00:32:34,286
Deal?

456
00:32:34,766 --> 00:32:35,726
Sounds good.

457
00:32:37,406 --> 00:32:38,286
Come on.

458
00:32:39,086 --> 00:32:40,086
Let's begin.

459
00:32:45,686 --> 00:32:47,046
Since you're a girl,

460
00:32:47,366 --> 00:32:48,686
we play three matches.

461
00:32:49,446 --> 00:32:50,806
Even if you manage to win a single round,

462
00:32:51,366 --> 00:32:52,686
I'll accept defeat.

463
00:32:54,726 --> 00:32:55,806
Since you're a man,

464
00:32:56,446 --> 00:32:57,606
even if you manage a win,

465
00:32:57,766 --> 00:32:58,686
I'll accept defeat.

466
00:32:59,046 --> 00:33:00,286
One round?

467
00:33:01,206 --> 00:33:02,726
- Alright, bring it on!
- She has no idea who she's dealing with!

468
00:33:03,726 --> 00:33:04,766
You know, right?

469
00:33:05,366 --> 00:33:07,206
Can't you see the
confidence in my eyes?

470
00:33:07,446 --> 00:33:08,366
Not a bit.

471
00:33:08,686 --> 00:33:09,606
It's only fair.

472
00:33:10,206 --> 00:33:11,126
You'll see.

473
00:33:13,606 --> 00:33:15,606
Look at her,
shaking before the game even starts!

474
00:33:15,686 --> 00:33:17,246
Well, it's expected
since you're the opponent.

475
00:34:06,766 --> 00:34:07,646
Show!

476
00:34:09,686 --> 00:34:10,686
What on earth is this?

477
00:34:12,406 --> 00:34:13,406
Lenin, we won.

478
00:34:13,446 --> 00:34:15,486
How could you possibly lose?
And to a girl, of all people?

479
00:34:15,566 --> 00:34:16,486
You idiot.

480
00:34:23,606 --> 00:34:24,446
Stop!

481
00:34:24,886 --> 00:34:25,846
Hey, Damodar!

482
00:34:26,806 --> 00:34:29,086
According to the terms,
you lost one round.

483
00:34:29,326 --> 00:34:30,206
Therefore,

484
00:34:30,326 --> 00:34:32,206
gambling
is officially banned this year!

485
00:34:32,326 --> 00:34:33,326
Got it?

486
00:34:33,646 --> 00:34:34,406
Move guys.

487
00:34:34,486 --> 00:34:35,846
- Move aside!
- Don't worry.

488
00:34:36,006 --> 00:34:36,806
You fool--

489
00:34:37,086 --> 00:34:38,206
It's alright, brother.

490
00:34:38,566 --> 00:34:39,566
Since you're a man,

491
00:34:39,966 --> 00:34:41,646
I'll give you another chance.

492
00:34:41,686 --> 00:34:42,486
Play!

493
00:34:59,886 --> 00:35:02,406
Do you see the
confidence in my eyes now?

494
00:35:28,406 --> 00:35:30,686
Where do you think you're going?

495
00:35:35,086 --> 00:35:37,286
Don't you dare
try your cheap tricks on me!

496
00:35:39,686 --> 00:35:40,486
Damn it!

497
00:35:44,486 --> 00:35:46,006
Why does a loser need a Dhoti?

498
00:35:46,006 --> 00:35:46,966
Pull! Pull it.

499
00:35:47,006 --> 00:35:48,966
Hold that. Hold that guys.

500
00:35:49,726 --> 00:35:51,006
- Hey!
- Oh! He's a man!

501
00:35:51,046 --> 00:35:52,646
Damodar brother!
You are too good.

502
00:35:55,326 --> 00:35:56,366
Go jump in a ditch.

503
00:35:56,406 --> 00:35:57,406
You piece of a crap.

504
00:36:16,726 --> 00:36:17,566
My love.

505
00:36:46,006 --> 00:36:47,886
If I tell my dad,
he might send you instead.

506
00:36:48,126 --> 00:36:49,366
I have some important business
in Tirupati tomorrow.

507
00:36:50,046 --> 00:36:51,486
Take me there safely
and bring me back.

508
00:36:51,886 --> 00:36:52,686
