1786
02:25:08,566 --> 02:25:10,686
<i>♪ I swear upon</i>
<i>These sacred wedding seats ♪</i>

1787
02:25:10,766 --> 02:25:12,886
<i>♪ I swear upon</i>
<i>The five sacred elements of nature! ♪</i>

1788
02:25:12,926 --> 02:25:15,046
<i>♪ Oh Chittedu Kondalu</i>
<i>Beat the traditional drums loud ♪</i>

1789
02:25:15,246 --> 02:25:16,086
My love!

1790
02:25:16,166 --> 02:25:19,326
<i>♪ Oh Janaki Bai, step forward</i>
<i>And hold the bride's long braid ♪</i>

1791
02:25:19,366 --> 02:25:23,966
<i>♪ O Lord of gentle smiles</i>
<i>Tie the sacred thread of marriage! ♪</i>

1792
02:26:02,246 --> 02:26:03,726
Hey, hey! Vasanth.

1793
02:26:04,926 --> 02:26:06,206
Where are you going?

1794
02:26:26,686 --> 02:26:27,566
What?

1795
02:26:28,646 --> 02:26:30,046
Are you afraid of death?

1796
02:26:31,846 --> 02:26:33,606
I was afraid too…

1797
02:26:34,726 --> 02:26:36,286
That I'd die without finishing you off.

1798
02:26:38,886 --> 02:26:40,526
I feel extremely happy today.

1799
02:26:40,726 --> 02:26:42,206
Hey! Hey, Lenin.

1800
02:26:42,406 --> 02:26:43,246
Let me go.

1801
02:26:44,166 --> 02:26:45,366
I beg you.

1802
02:26:47,966 --> 02:26:48,966
Hey, Vasanth.

1803
02:26:51,006 --> 02:26:53,486
I'm not angry with you at all.

1804
02:27:02,166 --> 02:27:03,406
It's just love…

1805
02:27:04,366 --> 02:27:05,566
for Bharathi.

1806
02:27:39,486 --> 02:27:41,646
It's been twelve days
since <i>Bharatham Mitta</i> began.

1807
02:27:42,726 --> 02:27:44,726
It means 288 hours.

1808
02:27:45,846 --> 02:27:48,006
17,280 minutes.

1809
02:27:49,246 --> 02:27:52,406
Ten lakhs, thirty six thousand
and eight hundred seconds.

1810
02:27:58,686 --> 02:28:01,326
Because of him, it felt like an instant.

1811
02:28:02,966 --> 02:28:04,086
If he were right here,

1812
02:28:04,926 --> 02:28:07,766
I’d ask him to give me moments
like these forever.

1813
02:28:18,566 --> 02:28:19,326
What do you say?

1814
02:28:20,286 --> 02:28:21,086
Will you give me?

1815
02:28:21,966 --> 02:28:22,766
My love!

1816
02:29:19,966 --> 02:29:24,366
Only two remained
after the Kurukshetra war, Rajendra.

1817
02:29:24,886 --> 02:29:26,526
<i>Dharma Raju</i> and a dog.

1818
02:29:27,486 --> 02:29:29,046
It's the same here.

